.TH VDISCD 8 "2026-10-05" "VLHE 1.0.1" "VLHE Manual"
.SH NAME
vdiscd \- serve VLHE's virtual CD-ROM drives from disc images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdiscd
.RB [ \-d
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR dsp ]
.RB [ \-s
.I file
.RB [ \-r ]]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RI [ image ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B vdisc.o
kernel module creates up to eight virtual CD-ROM drives,
.I /dev/vdisc0
upwards.
.B vdiscd
gives them their contents: it answers the drives' reads from disc
image files, and plays a disc's audio tracks through vsound, as an
ordinary program would, so CD audio is mixed with everything else -
or, when vsound is not loaded, straight to the sound card.
One
.B vdiscd
serves every drive.
.PP
It reads CUE sheets
.RI ( .cue ),
CloneCD images
.RI ( .ccd )
and ISO images
.RI ( .iso ).
A disc's CD-TEXT and CD+G graphics are read from the image by the
control centre's CD+G Viewer; the drives themselves give programs
neither.
.PP
An
.I image
named on the command line is put in drive
.I N
at start. Without one, and without
.BR \-r ,
.B vdiscd
starts with empty drives and waits for the control centre to attach
images; attaching, ejecting and moving
.I /dev/cdrom
all go through its control channel. It is normally started by
.B vlhe apply
or the control centre's Load button, and runs until it is sent
SIGTERM or SIGINT. Only one may run at a time.
.PP
It needs
.B vdisc.o
loaded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " N"
The drive the command-line
.I image
goes in, 0 to 7. Default 0.
.TP
.BI \-o " dsp"
Where CD audio goes. Default
.IR /dev/dsp .
VLHE starts it with one of two tags instead, looked up again each time
a track plays:
.B @VSOUND@
waits until vsound is loaded and its pump is ready and plays through
it;
.BI @VSOUND: path @
plays through vsound if it is ready, and otherwise to
.IR path ,
the sound card.
.TP
.BI \-s " file"
The drive state file: which image is in each drive, whether it comes
back at the next start, and which drive
.I /dev/cdrom
reaches. Kept up to date with every attach,
eject and change to Load at startup. The installed path is
.IR /var/lib/vlhe/state/drives .
.TP
.B \-r
At start, put back each drive's image that the state file marks to
be loaded at startup. Given unless
.B [CD Settings] DrivesAutoLoad
is 0.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet: no report per command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/vdiscctl
The control device
.B vdiscd
receives the drives' requests through.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vlhe/state/drives
The drive state; see
.BR vlhe.conf (5).
.TP
.I /var/run/vlhe/ctl/
Its process ID file, its control and reply channels, and the link
.I /dev/cdrom
points through.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped by a signal after running normally.
.TP
.B 1
Another
.B vdiscd
is running; the drive number is out of range; the image could not be
opened or attached;
.I /dev/vdiscctl
could not be opened (is
.B vdisc.o
loaded?); there was not enough memory; or the kernel interface failed
while running.
.TP
.B 2
A bad option, an option missing its value, or more than one image.
.SH EXAMPLES
Serve one image in drive 0, by hand:
.PP
.RS
vdiscd /home/me/discs/game.cue
.RE
.SH BUGS
Ejecting a disc that a program has open, or that is mounted, is
refused without saying who holds it.
.PP
Drives cannot be added while it runs; the number of drives is set
when
.B vdisc.o
loads.
